{"decl":"TriangleFree","line":8,"plain":"A k-colouring C of the edges of K_n has no monochromatic triangle: every colour class graph is 3-clique-free.","standard_concept":"triangle-free (monochromatic-triangle-free) edge colouring","matches_standard":"yes","note":""},
{"decl":"ForcesMonochromaticTriangle","line":12,"plain":"Every k-colouring of E(K_n) contains a monochromatic triangle.","standard_concept":"n ≥ R_k(3) (arrow property)","matches_standard":"yes","note":"For k = 0 and n ≥ 2 there are no colourings, so the property holds vacuously. This is irrelevant to the asymptotics."},
{"decl":"triangleRamseyNumber","line":15,"plain":"R_k(3) = the least n such that every k-colouring of K_n has a monochromatic triangle.","standard_concept":"multicolour Ramsey number R(3,…,3) with k colours","matches_standard":"yes","note":"sInf of a set of ℕ. The set is nonempty for k ≥ 1 by the finite Ramsey theorem, so there is no junk 0."}
],
