{"theorem":"triangleRamseyNumber_log_sharp_coefficients","line":36,"plain":"For every ε > 0, for all sufficiently large k, (1/4−ε)·k·log k ≤ log R_k(3) ≤ (1+ε)·k·log k."},
{"theorem":"triangleRamseyNumber_log_isTheta","line":45,"plain":"log R_k(3) = Θ(k log k) as k → ∞, i.e. R_k(3) = k^{Θ(k)}."}
